// ocsf-1.9-rescore arm (d), sysmon availability probe (judgement disclosed in RESULTS.md).
// Shipped package `microsoft`, entry `microsoft::windows::ocsf::normalize event, into=ocsf` as in the
// package's examples/windows-event-log-nxlog-to-ocsf.tql (mapping unedited). The corpus is flat
// pre-parsed Sysmon EID 1 JSON, the shape NXLog im_msvistalog emits with AddPrefix disabled, minus
// NXLog's own metadata. Shaping adds three collector-metadata constants a real NXLog record carries
// (SourceModuleType routes canonicalize to the NXLog adapter; SourceName/Channel name the provider),
// analogous to the June run's `_path = "conn"`.
from_file "/work/sysmon.corpus.jsonl" {
  read_json
}
this.SourceModuleType = "im_msvistalog"
this.SourceName = "Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon"
this.Channel = "Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
this = {event: this}
microsoft::windows::ocsf::normalize event, into=ocsf
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(ocsf))
this._id = unmapped.EventData._id?
write_ndjson
